  "funFact": "The ginkgo tree is the last surviving member of a plant group that was diverse during the age of dinosaurs. It is a gymnosperm like redwoods — both produce seeds without flowers — but ginkgos and conifers are on different branches of the gymnosperm tree. Ferns are even more distant, having diverged before seeds evolved at all.",
